Why Are Reclaim Wafers Important?

Reclaim wafers are refurbished monitor and dummy silicon wafers used in semiconductor manufacturing support processes. They are distinct from recovered failed production wafers intended to be returned to product manufacturing.

A typical reclaim process removes deposited films and contamination, restores surface geometry through grinding or polishing, performs high-purity cleaning and checks key quality parameters before the wafer is reused.

Cost Optimization Supports Market Growth

Semiconductor manufacturing involves substantial recurring material and operating costs. Reclaiming suitable monitor and dummy wafers can reduce the need to purchase new wafers for selected process-control and equipment-conditioning tasks.

The economic benefit depends on wafer condition, reclaim yield, required specifications and the number of reuse cycles supported by the process.

Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing Increases Quality Requirements

As wafer-fabrication processes become more demanding, reclaimed wafers must meet strict requirements for surface flatness, particles, metallic contamination and geometry.

Reclaim suppliers must maintain consistent cleaning and polishing processes while minimizing surface damage. Quality verification is essential because unsuitable wafers can compromise equipment monitoring and process-control activities.

